### Visualizing sequential residual learning

The following function plots either the prediction of an individual tree or the sum of several trees.

::: {#define-gradient-boosting-plot-function .cell execution_count=27}
``` {.python .cell-code code-fold="true" code-summary="Show code"}
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt


def plot_regression_predictions(
    regressors,
    X,
    y,
    ax,
    axes,
    style="-",
    label=None,
    data_style=".",
    data_label=None
):
    x_grid = np.linspace(
        axes[0],
        axes[1],
        500
    ).reshape(-1, 1)

    y_grid = sum(
        regressor.predict(x_grid)
        for regressor in regressors
    )

    ax.plot(
        X[:, 0],
        y,
        data_style,
        label=data_label
    )

    ax.plot(
        x_grid[:, 0],
        y_grid,
        style,
        linewidth=2,
        label=label
    )

    ax.axis(axes)
    ax.grid(alpha=0.25)

    if label is not None or data_label is not None:
        ax.legend(
            loc="upper center",
            fontsize=9
        )
```
